From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:57:09 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?WIP=20tegra-vde=20T124:=20per-slice=20SXE=200x6?=
 =?UTF-8?q?0/0x64/0xdc/0x50=20(t124=5Fmask=20bits=2028-31)=20=E2=80=94=20d?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ead=20end?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stock fn_04828 writes these per slice. Individually they are byte-identical
no-ops; together they fault. Kept behind bits 28-31 for reproducibility.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/nvidia/tegra-vde/h264.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/nvidia/tegra-vde/h264.c b/drivers/media/platform/nvidia/tegra-vde/h264.c
index e1716dd9f..094b44f99 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/nvidia/tegra-vde/h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/nvidia/tegra-vde/h264.c
@@ -568,6 +568,24 @@ static int tegra_vde_setup_hw_context(struct tegra_vde *vde,
 
 	tegra_vde_writel(vde, value, vde->sxe, 0x4C);
 
+	if (vde->soc->t124_layout) {
+		/*
+		 * Stock AVP microcode fn_04828: per-slice SXE registers that
+		 * mainline never writes. Bits 28-31 split them for testing
+		 * (28 = 0x60 ref counts, 29 = 0x64, 30 = 0xdc, 31 = 0x50).
+		 */
+		if (t124_mask & BIT(28))
+			tegra_vde_writel(vde, ctx->num_ref_idx_l0_active_minus1 << 22 |
+					 ctx->num_ref_idx_l1_active_minus1 << 27,
+					 vde->sxe, 0x60);
+		if (t124_mask & BIT(29))
+			tegra_vde_writel(vde, 0x00010000, vde->sxe, 0x64);
+		if (t124_mask & BIT(30))
+			tegra_vde_writel(vde, 0x04407500, vde->sxe, 0xDC);
+		if (t124_mask & BIT(31))
+			tegra_vde_writel(vde, 0x00000000, vde->sxe, 0x50);
+	}
+
 	value = 0x03800000;
 	value |= bitstream_data_size & GENMASK(19, 15);
 
